+/-- The successive `next_match` results of the `CharSearcher` of `needle` (core
+    str/pattern.rs, rustc 1.95): each occurrence of the needle's UTF-8 encoding
+    (found with `memchr` on one of its bytes, then compared), from the first. In
+    a valid UTF-8 haystack an occurrence of a char's encoding starts at a char
+    boundary: these are the byte ranges of the chars equal to the needle.
+    `next_match_back` (`memrchr` on its last byte) returns the same ranges from
+    the last. -/
